# 8. Conditional Rendering

Conditional rendering displays UI based on conditions.

### if/else

```jsx
function App() {
  const isLoggedIn = true;

  if (isLoggedIn) {
    return <h1>Welcome Back</h1>;
  }

  return <h1>Please Login</h1>;
}
```

### Ternary Operator

```jsx
const isLoggedIn = true;

return (
  <div>
    {isLoggedIn ? <h1>Dashboard</h1> : <h1>Login</h1>}
  </div>
);
```

### Logical AND

```jsx
const isAdmin = true;

return (
  <div>
    {isAdmin && <h1>Admin Panel</h1>}
  </div>
);
```

# 9. Lists and Keys

Use map() to render arrays.

```jsx
const students = [
  { id: 1, name: "Faruk" },
  { id: 2, name: "Rahim" },
  { id: 3, name: "Karim" }
];

function App() {
  return (
    <div>
      {students.map(student => (
        <h2 key={student.id}>{student.name}</h2>
      ))}
    </div>
  );
}
```

Key helps React identify list items efficiently.

Use stable unique IDs as keys.

